ll now cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. This is the clearest sign that equity can't fund its plan. Pellham had planned to raise 2027 capex by 18% (`utility-capex-2027`) and is Caldria's largest single buyer of grid equipment.\n- **Sector:** Equity markets have been less receptive generally. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size (`utility-credit`, Q3 2026).\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It plans a 12% capex increase. The sources don't show it attempting an equity raise. It did price a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so debt looks like its viable route.\n- **Debt as the alternative:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, but the market is open. That is the subject of the sibling debt-markets question (n5, n3).\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The sources are thin. I have no figures on total equity needs, current valuations or Norvane's funding gap.\n- The evidence covers only two sector offerings that were cut back and one that was withdrawn. Equity could reopen if conditions improve, but nothing here suggests that.\n- Small or downsized equity raises are still possible. Large ones like Pellham's C$2.4B don't look achievable now.","ttft_ms":2707,"type":"result","duration_ms":27322,"uuid":"7f8c606e-6232-4180-bda5-6bb508fadb0e","ttft_stream_ms":1516,"time_to_request_ms":97,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":27,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":2,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":47,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":73,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mi